{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f39f74c2","source":["# Enterprise SaQS Churn Capstone: Adoption & Value Realization\n","**Required Capstone Assignment 20.1 â€” Initial Report and Exploratory Data Analysis**\n","\n","**Business question:** Can account profile, adoption, engagement and value-realization signals help identify enterprise SaQS accounts at risk of churn or downgrade?\n","\n","**Target:** `churn` (1 = churned/downgraded; 0 = retained/renewed).  \n","**Data notice:** This is a synthetic teaching dataset of 50 accounts, not real customer telemetry. Results are illustrative only.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"1759f263","outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Original shape: (50, 16)\n"]},{"data":{"text/plain":["churn\n","0    45\n","1     5\n","Name: account_count, dtype: int64"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["import warnings\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n","from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\n","from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n","from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n","from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n","from sklearn.metrics import (recall_score, precision_score, average_precision_score,\n","    roc_auc_score, ConfusionMatrixDisplay, PrecisionRecallDisplay)\n","\n","RANDOM_STATE = 42\n","df = pd.read_csv('../data/saas_telemetry.csv')\n","print('Original shape:', df.shape)\n","display(df.head())\n","display(df.isna().sum().to_frame('missing_count'))\n","display(df['churn'].value_counts().rename('account_count'))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"cf919195","source":["## Data quality and cleaning\\nInspect missing values, duplicate account identifiers and potential numeric outliers. Outliers are flagged using the 1.5Ã—IQR rule; do not remove legitimate enterprise-scale values without business justification. Missing values are imputed inside the modeling pipeline to avoid leakage."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"afdee61f","outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Duplicate account IDs removed: 0\n"]},{"data":{"text/plain":["                                  missing_count\n","csat_score                                    2\n","api_calls_monthly                             1\n","executive_sponsor_qbr_attendance              1"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"text/plain":["                             feature  outlier_count   lower_bound   upper_bound\n","0             contract_tenure_months              0 -2.862500e+01  1.063750e+02\n","1           annual_recurring_revenue              7 -2.603125e+06  4.984475e+06\n","2                      seat_licenses              7 -1.326875e+03  3.174125e+03\n","3            license_utilization_pct              0  2.141250e-01  1.071125e+00\n","4                      dau_mau_ratio              0  4.250000e-03  9.942500e-01\n","5                core_modules_active              0 -1.500000e+00  1.050000e+01\n","6                  api_calls_monthly              4 -1.701500e+03  1.741450e+04\n","7        kpi_milestones_achieved_pct              0  7.962500e-02  1.262625e+00\n","8                automated_workflows              0 -1.000000e+00  1.070000e+02\n","9   executive_sponsor_qbr_attendance              0  5.000000e-01  4.500000e+00\n","10                        csat_score              0  1.500000e+00  5.500000e+00"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["duplicate_count = int(df['account_id'].duplicated().sum())\n","df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=['account_id']).copy()\n","print('Duplicate account IDs removed:', duplicate_count)\n","missing_summary = df.isna().sum().sort_values(ascending=False)\n","display(missing_summary[missing_summary > 0].to_frame('missing_count'))\n","\n","numeric_for_outliers = df.select_dtypes(include='number').columns.drop('churn')\n","outlier_rows = []\n","for column in numeric_for_outliers:\n","    q1, q3 = df[column].quantile([0.25, 0.75])\n","    iqr = q3 - q1\n","    lower, upper = q1 - 1.5 * iqr, q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n","    count = int(((df[column] < lower) | (df[column] > upper)).sum())\n","    outlier_rows.append({'feature': column, 'outlier_count': count,\n","                         'lower_bound': lower, 'upper_bound': upper})\n","outlier_summary = pd.DataFrame(outlier_rows)\n","display(outlier_summary)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ccc46fab","source":["## Feature engineering\\nCreate normalized commercial and adoption indicators. `account_id` is excluded from predictors to avoid treating an identifier as a signal."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"757d30a8","outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Model rows: 50 | churn prevalence: 0.1\n"]}],"source":["df['arr_per_seat'] = df['annual_recurring_revenue'] / df['seat_licenses'].replace(0, np.nan)\n","df['adoption_gap'] = 1 - df['license_utilization_pct']\n","df['value_deficit'] = 1 - df['kpi_milestones_achieved_pct']\n","df['utilization_band'] = pd.cut(\n","    df['license_utilization_pct'], [0, .4, .6, .8, 1.01],\n","    labels=['<40%', '40â€“60%', '60â€“80%', '>80%'], include_lowest=True)\n","target, id_column = 'churn', 'account_id'\n","X = df.drop(columns=[target, id_column])\n","y = df[target].astype(int)\n","print('Model rows:', len(df), '| churn prevalence:', round(y.mean(), 3))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9a21d30e","source":["## Exploratory data analysis\\m¹Q¡”™½±±½Ý¥¹œ¡…ÉÑÌ•á…µ¥¹”Ñ…É•Ð‰…±…¹”°¡ÕÉ¸‰äÑ¥•È°±¥•¹Í”ÕÑ¥±¥é…Ñ¥½¸°¹Õµ•É¥Œ½ÉÉ•±…Ñ¥½¹Ì°…¹ÕÍÑ½µ•ÈÍ…Ñ¥Í™…Ñ¥½¸½Ù…±Õ”É•…±¥é…Ñ¥½¸¸É½ÕÀ‘¥™™•É•¹•Ì…É”‘•ÍÉ¥ÁÑ¥Ù”…ÍÍ½¥…Ñ¥½¹Ì°¹½Ð…ÕÍ…°•™™•ÑÌ¸‰uô±ì‰•±±}ÑåÁ”ˆè‰½‘”ˆ°‰•á•ÕÑ¥½¹}½Õ¹ÐˆèÐ°‰¥ˆèˆÙ•˜ÔÌá„Àˆ°‰½ÕÑÁÕÑÌˆémì‰‘…Ñ„ˆéì‰Ñ•áÐ½Á±…¥¸ˆél‰¡ÕÉ¸€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€€À€€€€€€€Å